    "Proposition 1 predicts that the empirical SML is flatter than CAPM implies: high-beta assets earn lower risk-adjusted returns (negative CAPM alpha) and low-beta assets earn higher risk-adjusted returns (positive CAPM alpha). We test this by running Fama-MacBeth cross-sectional regressions of excess returns on lagged betas. In the first pass, a separate OLS regression is estimated for each month $t$:\n",
